Tuesday Update
* Trade Alert: Buy MSFT and GM calls* Nasdaq reverses and shoots higher ami=
d bargain hunting spreeStocks are sweeping higher today, led higher by a st=
rong surge in technology amid a sharp drop in government bond yields.The Do=
w Jones Industrial Average rose by 334 points, or 1.1%, to 32,136. S&amp;P =
500 was higher by 2.1% to 3,901 and Nasdaq up by 3.7% to 13,080. Consumer d=
iscretionary and healthcare were the other two biggest gainers while energy=
 was the sole decliner.Tesla (TSLA) is on-track a "strong trajectory" in Ch=
ina for March as it released "quite impressive" sales results in the region=
 last month, Wedbush analysts said. The firm delivered 18,3000 units for Fe=
bruary, or an 18% increase from January. The analysts said the company is o=
n track to deliver more than 200,000 vehicles in China for 2021. Shares sur=
ged by 15% intraday, propelling Nasdaq and S&amp;P higher higher.Stitch Fix=
 (SFIX) said carrier delays for its packages weighed on revenue in the fisc=
al second quarter and have continued into the current period, prompting a l=
ower outlook for full-year sales. Shares plunged by 28%.The 10-year yield d=
ropped 4.3 basis points to 1.55%, retreating from its highest level since J=
anuary 2020 on Monday.The National Federation of Independent Business's ind=
ex rebounded slightly to 95.8 in February from 95 in January, breaking a st=
ring of three straight declines since the election of President Joseph Bide=
n.Meanwhile, the Organization for Economic Cooperation and Development said=
 it expects a 3.9% growth in 2021 and 3.8% growth in 2022 for the Euro area=
's economy. The new projections were respectively 0.3% and 0.5% higher than=
 estimates set out in December.Portfolio: We came into today flat as orders=
 for DKS and BBBY calls did not fill yesterday. We now have two new ideas f=
or you.*NEW RECOMMENDATIONSGeneral Motors (GM) March 50 calls-- Symbol: GM2=
10319C00050000-- Order: Buy at $5.00 lmt day only-- If filled, set up to se=
ll half at $6.50 lmt gtc and half at $8.50 lmt gtc-- If filled, set stop at=
 $3.50 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Microsoft Corp.(MSFT) March 232.5=
0 calls-- Symbol: MSFT210319C00232500-- Order: Buy at $5.00 lmt day only-- =
If filled, set up to sell half at $6.50 lmt gtc and half at $8.60 lmt gtc--=
 If filled, set stop at $3.50 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET only*Thanks for=
 reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly options expiring=
 on the third Friday of the specified month unless otherwise noted. All sto=
ps are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise specified. All o=
rders are good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day only" orders e=
xpire at the close of the current session. Past results are no guarantee of=
